setup-language-title = Language and keyboard
setup-language-description = Choose your language and personal keyboard layout under System. The language applies at your next login. Apply the keyboard layout and try it in the test field.
setup-display-title = Display
setup-display-description = Choose an available resolution under System. Confirm each change within 15 seconds or it will be reverted. Changes last until you sign out.
setup-wifi-description = Find networks, select one and connect. Existing NetworkManager profiles are preserved.
setup-bluetooth-description = Find and pair your keyboard and mouse. Confirmation appears inside Rampi.
setup-account-title = Linux account
setup-account-description = Your Linux account and PAM determine your permissions. Change your password or sign out under System. Existing sudo permissions allow you to create further accounts in the embedded system terminal; new accounts receive no administrator rights.
setup-vpn-description = Connect Tailscale on this page and sign in with the provider if needed, or import and connect a personal WireGuard profile. Status reflects the actual service; routes apply system-wide.
setup-host-title = Windows host
setup-host-description = Add personal hosts and select the active Windows 11 Pro host. Windows needs no additional Rampi software for RDP.
setup-ssh-title = SSH key
setup-ssh-description = Create a personal key with OpenSSH inside Rampi or use an existing key. Independently verify the host fingerprint on the Windows host before accepting it. Transfer only the public key to the Windows account.
setup-stream-title = Desktop streaming
setup-stream-description = Set up Sunshine on the host. Open the streaming page in the Remote module, approve the displayed PIN in Sunshine and select an application. Your personal Linux keyring manages pairings.
setup-rdp-description = Windows 11 Pro must allow Remote Desktop. The host, Windows account and resolution come from your active profile.
setup-board-description = Choose a task source: local file, GitHub, Gitea, Trello, Jira, Asana or Notion. The three steps guide you through the source, personal access and connection check. Then open the board directly.
setup-finish-title = Finish
setup-finish-description = Skip any step and resume setup later. Finishing confirms only your setup walkthrough, not connectivity or compatibility.
